# Ansible LEMP Stack Deployment

## Project Status
✅ Project structure created  
✅ VirtualBox and Vagrant installed  
✅ VMs created and running (web01 @ 192.168.56.10, db01 @ 192.168.56.11)  
⚠️ Ansible on Windows (Python 3.13) has compatibility issues  
✅ Workaround: Use Docker or WSL for Ansible execution

## What Works
- Vagrant VMs are fully operational
- SSH connectivity between host and VMs
- Project structure with Ansible roles and playbooks
- All configuration files are ready

## Issues Encountered
1. Ansible on Windows with Python 3.13 has blocking I/O issues
2. Terminal inside VMs has input issues (common VirtualBox problem)

## Solutions Demonstrated
1. **Vagrant Configuration**: Automated VM provisioning
2. **Ansible Best Practices**: Role-based structure, inventory management
3. **Troubleshooting**: Handling plugin errors, network configuration

## Project Files
ansible-lemp-stack/
├── Vagrantfile # VM configuration
├── ansible.cfg # Ansible configuration
├── inventory/hosts.ini # Host inventory
├── playbooks/site.yml # Main playbook
├── roles/ # Ansible roles
│ ├── common/ # Common configuration
│ ├── webserver/ # Nginx + PHP setup
│ └── database/ # MariaDB setup
└── group_vars/ # Group variables

## How to Run (On Linux/macOS or Windows with WSL/Docker)
```bash
# 1. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/Kartik27baliyan/ansible-lemp-stack.git
cd ansible-lemp-stack

# 2. Start VMs
vagrant up

# 3. Run Ansible (using Docker if on Windows)
docker run --rm -it \
  -v $(pwd):/ansible \
  -w /ansible \
  williamyeh/ansible:alpine3 \
  ansible-playbook playbooks/site.yml

# 4. Verify deployment
curl http://192.168.56.10
